  "seed": "The user, 2026-09-30: dragging a layer should feel physical. The row you grab lifts and rides the pointer up and down, the rows around it move out of its way, and the gap they open is where it lands, drawn in at the depth it will join. Which half of which row the pointer is over decides it: the bottom half of a group's last child lands inside the group, the top half of the row under the group lands below it. This walk carries rows at Next defaults through the same drag the pointer drives: a plain reorder, into the foot of a group, out below a group, a carry called off with Escape, a shut group that springs open when the row rests on it, and a whole group moved, photographing each one mid-drag with the gap open, and checking the list after each drop.",
